meta {
  name: Import Referral Panels (Excel)
  type: http
  seq: 14
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/referral-panels/import-xlsx
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  file: @file(C:\path\to\referral-panels.xlsx)
}

tests {
  test("201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });
  test("reports total/created/skipped", function () {
    const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
    expect(data).to.have.property("total");
    expect(data).to.have.property("created");
    expect(data).to.have.property("skipped");
    expect(data.skipped).to.be.an("array");
  });
}

docs {
  Bulk-import referring panels from an uploaded `.xlsx` workbook — the bulk
  counterpart to **Create Referral Panel**. Tenant comes from the JWT.

  Form field name is **`file`**. Only
  `application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet` (`.xlsx`)
  is accepted; anything else → 422 `INVALID_UPLOAD_FILE`. Max size 10 MB.

  ## Expected file format

  ONE data row = ONE referral panel. The header row is located by content (the
  first of the first ~10 rows containing a **"Referring Panel Name"** column),
  so a blank leading row is fine. Every column of the referral-panel template is
  mapped; headers are matched case-insensitively and tolerant of `*`, spaces and
  punctuation (`"TDS %"`, `"Referring Panel Name*"`, `"Incentive / Bonus %"` all
  match).

  Columns:
  - **Basic:** Panel Code, Referring Panel Name*, Short Name, Client Type*
    (CASH/PREPAID/POSTPAID), Referral Panel Settings ID (the settings `_id`),
    Status (ACTIVE/INACTIVE).
  - **Address:** Address Line 1/2, City, State, Country, PIN Code, GST Number,
    PAN Number.
  - **Bank:** Account Holder Name, Bank Name, Account Number, IFSC Code.
  - **Contacts (flat trios):** Director / Accession Person / Registration Person
    / Logistics Person / Accounts Person — Name, Mobile, Email each.
  - **Lab lists:** Lab Test List ID, Lab Panel List ID (the branch list `_id`s).
    Applied only when a **Branch ID** is supplied on the row.
  - **Commission:** Commission Applicable, Commission Type
    (PERCENTAGE/SLAB_BASED/FIXED_AMOUNT), Commission % on Lab Test List,
    Commission % on Lab Panel List, Fixed Type (ORDER_WISE/MONTHLY/QUARTERLY/
    HALF_YEARLY/ANNUALLY), Fixed Amount, and the single slab triple
    **Slab Based - Monthly Business From / To / Commission %**.
  - **TDS:** TDS Applicable, TDS %.
  - **Payment & incentive:** Payment Cycle (NA/MONTHLY/…), Payment Mode
    (BANK_TRANSFER/CASH/CHEQUE), Monthly Target Amount, Incentive Bonus
    Applicable, and the single bonus triple **Incentive Bonus - Monthly Business
    From / To** + **Incentive / Bonus %**.
  - **Other:** Remarks, Branch ID (the branch `_id` the panel belongs to).

  Referral Panel Settings, Branch and both Lab Lists are supplied as **IDs**
  (either in a dedicated `… ID` column or in the corresponding named column).
  Each row supports ONE commission slab and ONE bonus slab.

  ## Behaviour — CREATE-ONLY, SKIP-AND-REPORT

  - Each row is validated against the create rules and then created via the same
    logic as **Create Referral Panel** (system `RP-…` code, commission/incentive
    validation, settings/branch checks, per-branch list assignment).
  - An invalid or **duplicate** (name / panel code) row is **skipped** and
    reported — valid rows still import. Response `201` →
    `{ "total": <rows read>, "created": <count>,
    "skipped": [ { "rowNumber": N, "name": ..., "panelCode": ...,
    "reason": "<why>" }, ... ] }`. `skipped` is `[]` on a fully clean import.
  - The ONE exception: a **file-level structural failure** (unreadable file,
    missing "Referring Panel Name"/"Client Type" header, or no data rows)
    rejects the whole upload as 400 `REFERRAL_PANEL_IMPORT_INVALID_FILE` with
    nothing created.
}
